{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.QuantumGapCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.QuantumGapCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.quantum_gap_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.quantum_gap_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L92-L102","doc":"**Quantum gap collapse (combined)**: Under the classical limit\nq → 1, the Planck constant vanishes and the Reeb period diverges.\n\nThe remaining two degenerations (Jackson q-derivative → ordinary\nderivative, braiding → symmetric swap) are categorical statements\nencoded in `ClassicalLimitFunctor.braiding_trivializes`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:quantum-gap-collapse","label":"thm:quantum-gap-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reeb_period_tendsto_atTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reeb_period_tendsto_atTop","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L71-L90","doc":"**Quantum gap collapse (part 2)**: |Ω_q| → ∞ as q → 1⁺.\n\nSince Ω(q) = ℏ(q)⁻¹ and ℏ(q) → 0⁺ from the right,\nthe Reeb period diverges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**Quantum gap collapse (part 1)**: ℏ_q → 0 as q → 1⁺.\n\nSince ℏ(q) = 1 - q⁻¹ is continuous and ℏ(1) = 0, this follows\nfrom continuity of subtraction and inversion at q = 1 ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L56-L58","doc":"For q > 1, ℏ(q) ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_pos","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L50-L54","doc":"For q > 1, ℏ(q) > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L46-L48","doc":"ℏ(1) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reebPeriod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reebPeriod","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L43-L44","doc":"The Reeb period as a plain real function: Ω(q) = (1 - q⁻¹)⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.planck","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L39-L41","doc":"The Planck constant as a plain real function: ℏ(q) = 1 - q⁻¹.\nArchimedean specialisation of the formal `1 - q⁻¹` to real `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/quantum-gap-collapse.lean#L29-L35","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. The\nalgebraic indeterminate lives here; the analytic degenerations\nbelow are stated after the archimedean specialisation `ι : R_q → ℝ`,\n`q ↦ q₀`, since `nhdsWithin`/`atTop`/ordering require an ordered\ntopological field (§7c: archimedean constructs ⇒ `ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}